    "stem": "Ojas opens a dried pea seed and finds two cotyledons. The seedling later has netted leaf veins and a thick central root. He also opens a rice grain and finds one cotyledon. In class he learns that two cotyledons mark a dicotyledon (reticulate venation, taproot) and one cotyledon marks a monocotyledon (parallel venation, fibrous roots).\n\nAnswer both parts.",
